    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — 11 PASS, 8 FAIL.\n\nThe dominant defect is a **stale graph-node rendering bug**: the React Flow nodes never receive updated model data, so level/weight/enabled controls keep showing their original values even though the underlying model recalculates correctly. This cascades into several failures (FT-4, FT-5, FT-7, IX-20), most damagingly making the disable toggle irreversible and letting a later edit clobber an earlier one.\n\nOther notable failures:\n- **FT-8** — \"Save Current\" is a dead button; there is no custom-template capture and no My Templates collection.\n- **FT-11** — \"Model Saved\" toast is cosmetic; nothing is persisted (storage empty), edits vanish on reopen.\n- **FT-7** — applying a template swaps the header/metrics but not the graph.\n- **IX-19** — the initially selected Recruitment scenario loads with zeroed adjustments and running it is a no-op until you switch tabs and back.\n- **CT-16** — the \"critical path\" is a set of high-weight competencies, not a connected path; it disagrees with graph highlighting after a weight change and retains disabled competencies.\n\nSearch/filtering, the graph's directed weighted presentation with pan/zoom/drag, scenario switching, simulation with correct 1–5 level and 10–100% weight clamping, live coverage updates, and the risk-gap alert all worked as specified."
  }
}
